Sol. (b)** Given that, \(\frac{a_{1} + a_{2} + \ldots + a_{p}}{a_{1} + a_{2} + \ldots + a_{q}} = \frac{p^{3}}{q^{3}}\)

\(\Rightarrow \ \frac{\frac{p}{2}\left\lbrack 2a_{1} + (p - 1)d \right\rbrack}{\frac{q}{2}\left\lbrack 2a_{2} + (q - 1)d \right\rbrack} = \frac{p^{3}}{q^{3}}\)

where, \(d\) is a common difference of an AP.

\(\begin{matrix}
 \Rightarrow & \frac{2a_{1} + (p - 1)d}{2a_{2} + (q - 1)d} = \frac{p^{2}}{q^{2}} \\
 \Rightarrow & \frac{a_{1} + (p - 1)\frac{d}{2}}{a_{2} + (q - 1)\frac{d}{2}} = \frac{p^{2}}{q^{2}}
\end{matrix}\)

On putting \(p = 11\) and \(q = 41\), we get

\(\Rightarrow \ \begin{matrix}
 & \frac{a_{1} + (11 - 1)\frac{d}{2}}{a_{2} + (41 - 1)\frac{d}{2}} = \frac{(11)^{2}}{(41)^{2}} \\
 & \frac{a_{1} + 5d}{a_{2} + 20d} = \frac{121}{1681} \Rightarrow \frac{a_{6}}{a_{21}} = \frac{121}{1681}
\end{matrix}\)

